# 30. MANDATORY QUALITY AND ACCEPTANCE TESTS

Before claiming that the platform is ready, test actual workflows.

### Member tests

- A member can create an account and sign in.
- The member can find accurate gym information.
- The member can browse actual equipment records.
- A scanned QR code opens the correct asset.
- The member can distinguish operational equipment from unavailable equipment.
- A member can submit an equipment fault report.
- A member can view published class times.
- A member can book and cancel a class.
- A member can view membership terms.
- A member can control social visibility.
- A member can make and manage friend requests.
- A member can report or block abusive users.
- A member can receive relevant notifications.
- A member can submit and track a support ticket.

### Staff tests

- Authorized staff can update permitted records.
- Unauthorized roles cannot edit restricted data.
- Equipment reports create maintenance work orders.
- Critical safety reports trigger the correct workflow.
- Staff can assign maintenance tasks.
- Work orders maintain their history.
- Restricted equipment cannot be falsely represented as available.
- Cleaning and inventory tasks can be tracked.
- Staff actions appear in appropriate audit logs.

### Owner tests

- An owner can manage membership records.
- An owner can manage classes and trainer schedules.
- Booking capacity is enforced.
- Payment status is verified.
- Financial reports distinguish pending and completed transactions.
- Business analytics use the correct time period.
- Branch permissions work correctly.
- Different gym organizations remain isolated.

### Platform tests

- Search works.
- Filters work.
- Buttons perform their stated actions.
- Data persists after refresh.
- Authentication and permissions are enforced server-side.
- Failure states are understandable.
- Network interruptions do not create duplicate payments or bookings.
- Mobile layouts work.
- Accessibility checks are performed.
- Database migrations are reproducible.
- Backups and recovery procedures are documented.
- Security-sensitive operations are logged.
- Critical workflows have automated tests.

Deliver a transparent test report listing passed checks, failed checks, incomplete integrations, outstanding risks, and next steps.

