Do not generate dead buttons, fake real-time indicators, fabricated machine statuses, fake payment confirmations, or meaningless analytics.

Where an integration requires external credentials, build the supported integration boundary, document the necessary environment variables, and state that configuration is still required.

Where live data is unavailable, provide useful manual functionality and clearly labeled demonstration data.

Do not call the product production-ready unless the necessary security, operational, integration, and acceptance checks have actually succeeded.

